\chapter{Results\label{results}}

\section{The \jlc}

If the \jlc is produced by fragmentation, no dependence on collision system or system size would be expected.  The particle ratios of the \jlc should be consistent with what was observed in \pp collisions since \pp collisions are expected to be dominated by jet production at high-\pT.  The \jly should increase with \pttrig because higher \pT trigger particles come on average from higher energy jets and the spectra of particles in the \jlc should be harder than that observed in the inclusive.  Studies of the \jly as a function of collision system and energy were done for unidentified hadrons for \Cu and \Au collisions at \sNNsixtytwo and \sNNtwohundred to determine whether the data are consistent with the \jlc being produced by fragmentation.

