\section{\myomega triggered correlations}

\myomega triggered correlations were statistically limited even in \Au \cite{Abelev:2007zp,betya}.  To minimize the effects of statistical fluctuations, the detector acceptance corrections were determined using \myxi distributions in azimuth and pseudorapidity.  Since statistical fluctuations were much larger than track losses due to track merging, track merging corrections were not applied.  To investigate the feasibility of studies of \myomega triggered correlations in \Cu at \sNNtwohundred, kinematic cuts were varied to find the cuts which maximize the signal to background ratio.  Lowering the lower limit on \ptassoc or \pttrig increases the statistics, however, it also increases the combinatorial background.  \omegabary and \aomegabary were added in order to increase statistics.

